style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 67.8pt; border-bottom: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 223.9pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;Net deferred income tax liabilities&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 1.45pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 61.2pt; border-top: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); border-bottom: 1.5pt double rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;(39,821,701)&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 1.45pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 1.45pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 67.8pt; border-top: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); border-bottom: 1.5pt double rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;(35,130,775)&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 223.9pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 1.45pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 61.2pt; border-top: 1.5pt double rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 1.45pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 1.45pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 67.8pt; border-top: 1.5pt double rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 			&lt;/table&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="width: 50.75pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span&gt;The TCJA includes significant changes affecting regulated public utilities, such as NY Transco. Substantially all of the provisions of the TCJA are effective for taxable years beginning after December 31, 2017. The TCJA reduces the corporate federal income tax rate from 35% to 21%. The specific provision related to regulated public utilities in the TCJA generally allows the continued deductibility of interest expense, does not allow for full expensing for tax purposes of certain property acquired after September 27, 2017, and continues certain rate normalization requirements for accelerated depreciation benefits.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;In accordance with the accounting rules for income taxes, the tax effects of changes in tax laws are to be recognized in the period in which the law is enacted and deferred tax assets and liabilities are to be re-measured at the enacted tax rate expected to apply when temporary differences are to be realized or settled. In accordance with the accounting rules for regulated operations, the change in deferred taxes was recorded as a regulatory liability at December 31, 2017, for approximately $5.1 million.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-indent: -28.8pt; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial Bold&amp;quot;; font-weight: bold"&gt;7.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 20.46pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company is subject to various legal proceedings arising out of the ordinary course of its business. The Company does not consider any of such proceedings to be material, individually or in the aggregate, to its business or likely to result in a material adverse effect on its results of operations, financial position, or cash flows.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company has entered into agreements with entities to provide engineering, procurement, construction and project management services related to the Dover PAR Station and Propel Project. These agreements extend until project completion and acceptance (the completion for Dover PAR Station was in December 2025 and the expected completion for the Propel Project is in 2030) unless terminated earlier without penalty. The agreements cover approximately 67% and 9%, respectively, of the work related to these projects.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-indent: -28.8pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial Bold&amp;quot;; font-weight: bold"&gt;8.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 20.46pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;NYISO Revenues&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company receives all its revenues from NYISO, which collects the Company's revenue requirement from load serving entities in New York, including the Company's New York State utility affiliates. Company transmission project costs are allocated to transmission districts or load zones as determined by NYISO and filed with the FERC. Accordingly, revenue collected by NYISO on behalf of the Company is collected from the customers of these affiliates consistent with the allocation methodology.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Transactions with Affiliated Companies&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Consolidated Edison Company of New York, Inc. (&amp;quot;CECONY&amp;quot;), Central Hudson Gas &amp;amp; Electric Corporation (&amp;quot;CHG&amp;amp;E&amp;quot;), National Grid (&amp;quot;Grid&amp;quot;), New York State Electric &amp;amp; Gas Corporation (&amp;quot;NYSEG&amp;quot;) and Orange &amp;amp; Rockland Utilities, Inc. (&amp;quot;O&amp;amp;R&amp;quot;), affiliates of the Company, provide various services to the Company in the ordinary course of business, including executive and administrative, financial (including accounting and tax), information technology and operational and maintenance services on some of its transmission assets. During 2025, the Company recorded $2.5 million of expenses for costs billed by affiliated companies, which are included in Operation and maintenance, General and administrative and Taxes other than income taxes for $0.3, $0.2 and $2.0 million, respectively. During 2024, the Company recorded $3.2 million of expenses for costs billed by affiliated companies, which are included in Operation and maintenance, General and administrative and Taxes other than income taxes for $0.6, $0.6 and $2.0 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;During 2025 and 2024, the Company incurred costs for the Segment B Project from CECONY, CHG&amp;amp;E, Grid, NYSEG and O&amp;amp;R, which were charged to Utility plant. The amount charged to Utility plant in 2025 and 2024 was $2.9 and $2.3 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Accounts payable to affiliated companies totaled $24.0 and $21.3 million as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively, which included costs related to Utility plant of $8.9 and $8.2 million as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-indent: -28.8pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial Bold&amp;quot;; font-weight: bold"&gt;9.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 20.46pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Joint Development Agreement&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;On April 23, 2023, the Company entered into a joint development agreement (the &amp;quot;JDA&amp;quot;) with NYPA to develop the Propel Project (refer to Note 1), which had an estimated cost of $2.8 billion. In accordance with the JDA, NYPA currently has a financial obligation of $0.5 billion towards the Propel Project, with the remaining $2.3 billion as the financial obligation of the Company. NYPA also has a right to increase its investment to 30% of the total cost for the Propel Project.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Additionally, according to the JDA, the financial ownership percentages of the Propel Project, which include all project costs incurred, are based on the financial obligations of NYPA and the Company. As of December 31, 2025, the financial ownership percentages are calculated as 17.8% for NYPA and 82.2% for the Company. In the event that costs incurred and recorded on the Company's books are more or less than the amount that should be allocated to maintain the 82.2% financial ownership percentage, the Company will receive from or reimburse NYPA the difference in order to maintain the financial ownership percentages. As of December 31, 2025, the Company has recorded a project cost reimbursement from NYPA in the amount of $12.9 million, which is included in Miscellaneous current and accrued assets.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-indent: -28.8pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial Bold&amp;quot;; font-weight: bold"&gt;10.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 14.9pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Preliminary Survey and Investigation Charges&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Preliminary Survey and Investigation Charges (Electric account 183) are costs associated with the development of solutions in response to the NYISO's PPTPP solicitation to address the NYC Offshore Wind Export Public Policy Transmission Need (the &amp;quot;NYC OSW PPTN&amp;quot;) as declared by the NYSPSC on June 22, 2023 in Case 22-E-0633.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;On July 17, 2025, the NYSPSC issued an order in the same docket to withdraw (i.e., cancel) the NYC OSW PPTN effective immediately (&amp;quot;NYC OSW PPTN Cancellation&amp;quot;). As a result of the NYC OSW PPTN Cancellation, the Company recorded a write-off in the amount of $12.7 million in 2025, which is included in Other Deductions (account 426.5) on the Statement of Income. The impairment represents the total costs incurred associated with the NYC OSW PPTN, other than $10 million of costs associated with the purchase of manufacturing capacity slot reservations for the manufacture of high voltage converter station equipment (the &amp;quot;Slot Reservations&amp;quot;) and $2.2 million of NYISO deposits related to the NYC OSW PPTN, for which the Company received reimbursement from the NYISO in January 2026. The costs that were impaired cannot be repurposed for another project, sold, or recovered through the Company's formula rate, and include engineering fees, contracting fees, permitting fees, project study fees, legal fees, and labor costs.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Slot Reservations are set to expire on November 30, 2026, with the possibility to extend the expiration date. Fair value of the Slot Reservations is based on current market conditions, less the estimated cost to sell. As the resulting net fair value of the Slot Reservations exceeds the carrying value, no loss was recorded.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;As a result of the NYC OSW PPTN Cancellation, the Company's management committed to a plan to sell the Slot Reservations to a third party through a broker and has accounted for the assets, along with the NYISO deposits, in Miscellaneous Current and Accrued Assets as of December 31, 2025.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-indent: -28.8pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial Bold&amp;quot;; font-weight: bold"&gt;11.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 14.9pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Subsequent Events&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company has evaluated subsequent events and transactions through April 13, 2026, the date of issuance of these financial statements.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 28.8pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;div style="clear: both"&gt; 				&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center"&gt; 					&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 				&lt;/p&gt; 				&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 7pt"&gt; 					&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 				&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;/div&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
