        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-67_329912_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">See Page 328 for details.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-114_329906_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource">Original value: N</link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-121_336135_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>On July 1, 2025, Kathleen A. Carrigan, the Company's VP - General Counsel and Regulatory Affairs, officially retired from the Company.<br />Aubrey Roman, a Partner with the Albany, NY based law firm Harris Beach Murtha, assumed the responsibilities of this position on an interim<br />basis following Ms. Carrigan's retirement.<br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-129_329907_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p><span style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"> Mr. Caso is the Vice President - Budget, Finance and Accounting as an employee of a third party.</span><br /></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-274_329911_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">There were no inventory adjustments resulting from periodic physical inventories, write-offs or obsolete material for year ended December 31, 2024.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-282_329909_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><table class="e-rte-table" style="width: 100%; min-width: 0"><tr><td class="" style="width: 50%">Operating revenue per line 2</td><td style="width: 50%" class="">$134,506,373</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 50%" class="">Rate year 2023 true-up</td><td style="width: 50%" class=""><span style="text-decoration: underline">$124,640</span></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 50%" class="">Rate year 2024 operating revenue</td><td style="width: 50%" class="">$134,631,013</td></tr></table><p><br /></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-332_329905_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>ER15-572, ER24-232, ER25-885 an dER26-893, which are recovered under the NYISO OATT.</p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-455_336151_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><table class="e-rte-table" style="width: 100%; min-width: 0"><tr><td class="" style="width: 50%">Operating revenues per line 2</td><td style="width: 50%" class="">$154,959,190</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 50%" class="">Prior Rate Year true-up</td><td style="width: 50%" class=""><span style="text-decoration: underline">$421,381</span></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 50%" class="">Rate Year 2025 operating revenues</td><td style="width: 50%" class="">$155,380,571</td></tr></table><p><br /></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-857_336152_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">There were no inventory adjustments resulting from periodic physical inventories, write-offs or obsolete material for year ended December 31, 2025.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-933_334506_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">See Page 328 for details.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1000_334507_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">New York Independent System Operator ("NYISO") OATT, Section 6.13, Rate Schedule 13 and Section 13 and Section 36, Attachment DD.</span><br/></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1020_334514_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">In 2022, the Respondent entered into a 99-year lease with Orange &amp; Rockland Utility, which allowed for the Respondent to use the rights-of-way related to the transmission corridors.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1021_334510_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">Amount represents land rights.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1022_334512_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">In 2021, the Respondent entered into a 99-year lease with National Grid, and in 2022 with Consolidated Edison Company of NY, which allowed for the Respondent to use the rights-of-way related to the transmission corridors. The cost of the use and occupancy rights associated with the lease is included in land rights for the Respondent.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1023_334513_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">In 2022, the Respondent entered into an agreement to purchase easements from Central Hudson, which allowed for the Respondent to use the rights-of-way related to the transmission corridors.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1024_334511_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">Amount represents land rights.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1025_334515_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">In 2021, the Respondent entered into a 99-year lease with National Grid, and in 2022 with Consolidated Edison Company of NY, which allowed for the Respondent to use the rights-of-way related to the transmission corridors. The cost of the use and occupancy rights associated with the lease is included in land rights for the Respondent.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1036_334508_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">In 2016 the Respondent entered into a 99-year lease with Consolidated Edison Company of New York, Inc., which included the right for the Respondent to use the easterly side of the existing double circuit transmission structures, running from the Sugarloaf Substation to the Rock Tavern Substation, for the construction of a second 345kV transmission line and use of the rights-of-way related to the transmission corridor. The cost for the use and occupancy rights associated with the lease is included in land rights and towers and fixtures.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1037_334509_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto">In 2016 the Respondent entered into a 99-year lease with New York State Electric &amp; Gas Corporation, which included the right for the Respondent to use certain structures on the Fraser to Coopers Corner transmission line (FCC 33 Line) and the use of the rights-of-way related to the transmission corridor and a new series capacitor yard in Delhi, NY. The cost of the use and occupancy rights associated with the lease is included in land rights and towers and fixtures for the Respondent.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1626_336154_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>Amount represents property taxes charged to account 408.1 that were billed by affiliates and included in account 234, Accounts payable to associated companies.</p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1651_336157_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto">Florida income tax charged to account 409.2.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1652_336158_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto">Massachusetts income tax charged to account 409.2.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1653_336155_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>Federal income tax charged to account 409.2.</p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1654_336156_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto">NYS income tax charged to account 409.2.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1655_336159_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto">NYC income tax charged to account 409.2.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
    </link:footnoteLink>
</xbrl>